4913
05:21:19.512 --> 05:21:23.362
His situation shows how disability, inaccessible housing, poverty,

4914
05:21:23.472 --> 05:21:27.442
and stigma intersect, and how easily a person like him could

4915
05:21:27.472 --> 05:21:28.761
be moved on under this bill.

4916
05:21:30.092 --> 05:21:32.832
This bill does not address any of those issues.

4917
05:21:32.852 --> 05:21:36.712
Instead, it gives police the power to move disabled people away from the places

4918
05:21:36.752 --> 05:21:40.452
where they feel safest and where their support networks are located.

4919
05:21:42.552 --> 05:21:46.492
Point two, epilepsy is invisible in homelessness policy, but it absolutely

4920
05:21:46.532 --> 05:21:47.712
is present in reality.

4921
05:21:48.532 --> 05:21:51.942
Epilepsy is one of Aotearoa's most common long-term neurological

4922
05:21:52.012 --> 05:21:52.652
disabilities,

4923
05:21:53.552 --> 05:21:57.232
yet it is almost entirely invisible in homelessness reporting, disability

4924
05:21:57.312 --> 05:22:01.052
data, and policy design. That invisibility is dangerous.

4925
05:22:02.332 --> 05:22:06.172
International research shows epilepsy rates among homeless adults are three to

4926
05:22:06.212 --> 05:22:08.772
four times higher than in the general population.

4927
05:22:09.832 --> 05:22:13.072
Homelessness increases seizure frequency through sleep deprivation,

4928
05:22:13.472 --> 05:22:17.032
stress, exposure to cold, and inconsistent access to

4929
05:22:17.072 --> 05:22:17.632
medication.

4930
05:22:18.792 --> 05:22:22.192
Homeless adults with epilepsy have two to three times higher mortality,

4931
05:22:22.532 --> 05:22:26.212
including increased risk of sudden unexpected death in epilepsy,

4932
05:22:26.952 --> 05:22:27.532
