5454
05:57:17.072 --> 05:57:20.892
So my name is Vic, and I am the co-lead of the

5455
05:57:20.932 --> 05:57:23.982
Coalition to End Women's Homelessness, alongside Dr.

5456
05:57:24.312 --> 05:57:27.972
Cathy Irwin. I'm joined by our Collective Impact lead, Amanda

5457
05:57:28.012 --> 05:57:30.812
Kelly, and the coalition includes Dr.

5458
05:57:31.052 --> 05:57:34.952
Jo Cribb, who is the chair of the Wellington Homeless Women's Trust, Helen

5459
05:57:34.992 --> 05:57:38.852
Robinson, the Auckland City Missioner, Carolyn Hidewini, who leads Te

5460
05:57:38.872 --> 05:57:42.712
Whare Tīāki Porirua Maori Women's Refuge, and also

5461
05:57:42.752 --> 05:57:45.612
Jill Hawkey, who leads the Christchurch Methodist Mission.

5462
05:57:47.732 --> 05:57:51.152
What brought us together three years ago to start the coalition was a

5463
05:57:51.192 --> 05:57:55.172
recognition that there is a complete void of

5464
05:57:55.232 --> 05:57:59.012
policy and funding response to the specific needs of women

5465
05:57:59.112 --> 05:58:00.732
when it comes to homelessness.

5466
05:58:02.051 --> 05:58:05.032
We have been funded and supported to

5467
05:58:05.092 --> 05:58:09.052
undertake and commission research to work with the sector

5468
05:58:09.112 --> 05:58:12.362
to strengthen their practice in response to women's

5469
05:58:12.432 --> 05:58:15.441
homelessness and to advocate for change.

5470
05:58:15.932 --> 05:58:18.392
And it's on that last point that we are here

5471
05:58:18.452 --> 05:58:22.312
today. We're submitting because of the insight and

5472
05:58:22.432 --> 05:58:26.372
expertise of our colleagues, and also of the people with

5473
05:58:26.452 --> 05:58:29.352
lived experience who have shared their stories with us

5474
05:58:29.912 --> 05:58:33.772
through the providers on the frontline, the outreach services, and

5475
05:58:33.872 --> 05:58:37.472
also our research. Our initial research included the stories of

5476
05:58:37.612 --> 05:58:40.432
37 women who have experienced homelessness.

5477
05:58:42.132 --> 05:58:46.092
We are also here because we believe that we, as New Zealanders, must look to our

5478
05:58:46.132 --> 05:58:49.482
best and strongest instincts for care and

5479
05:58:49.532 --> 05:58:52.172
manaakitanga in order to end homelessness.

5480
05:58:52.612 --> 05:58:56.572
And it is our firm belief that the Move On orders, as they are

5481
05:58:56.612 --> 05:59:00.312
proposed, represent anything but that

5482
05:59:00.672 --> 05:59:04.492
best instinct. I'll hand to Amanda to talk you through

5483
05:59:04.532 --> 05:59:05.172
our submission.

5484
05:59:06.712 --> 05:59:10.332
Kia ora koutou. Ko Amanda Kelly toku ingoa, and I work as

5485
05:59:10.352 --> 05:59:14.192
Collective Impact lead at the Coalition to End Women's Homelessness.

5486
05:59:14.912 --> 05:59:18.572
Thank you, Vic. From a gendered perspective, we are extremely

5487
05:59:18.612 --> 05:59:22.572
concerned about how this proposed bill will impact women

5488
05:59:22.752 --> 05:59:26.672
experiencing homelessness, in particular wahine Maori, who

5489
05:59:26.732 --> 05:59:30.312
make up around one third of the 57,000 women

5490
05:59:30.732 --> 05:59:33.472
who are homeless across this country.

5491
05:59:33.532 --> 05:59:37.392
We are also deeply concerned about the impact that this will have

5492
05:59:37.452 --> 05:59:41.052
on their children and young people, as young as

5493
05:59:41.152 --> 05:59:44.712
14 years of age. And for children and young people, being on the

5494
05:59:44.852 --> 05:59:48.812
street is the consequence of circumstances that is way

5495
05:59:48.872 --> 05:59:50.132
beyond their control.

5496
05:59:51.464 --> 05:59:54.784
Our research tells us that women experience homelessness

5497
05:59:57.204 --> 06:00:00.784
very differently. They are extremely vulnerable, and they are

5498
06:00:00.864 --> 06:00:04.624
often less visible, and they have survival

5499
06:00:04.724 --> 06:00:08.384
mechanisms like we just heard in the previous submission from

5500
06:00:08.464 --> 06:00:08.804
Bea.

5501
06:00:09.844 --> 06:00:13.824
We are concerned that move-on orders risk making women's homelessness

5502
06:00:13.904 --> 06:00:17.304
even more invisible by pushing women to the

5503
06:00:17.384 --> 06:00:21.324
margins rather than bringing women closer to the support

5504
06:00:21.334 --> 06:00:22.964
and safety they may need.

5505
06:00:24.164 --> 06:00:27.994
Move-on orders may disrupt trusted relationships and connections with

5506
06:00:28.044 --> 06:00:31.804
key outreach workers, reduce access to vital healthcare

5507
06:00:32.244 --> 06:00:36.064
and housing services, increase isolation, and force

5508
06:00:36.164 --> 06:00:39.944
women and children into more dangerous and harmful situations.

5509
06:00:41.164 --> 06:00:44.964
I want to take a moment to acknowledge Wendy Proffitt

5510
06:00:45.004 --> 06:00:48.904
and her late daughter, Caitlin, whose story was shared

5511
06:00:48.944 --> 06:00:50.604
this week by RNZ.

5512
06:00:52.184 --> 06:00:56.054
Caitlin's heartbreaking story reminds us that

5513
06:00:56.104 --> 06:00:59.854
housing is the foundation of health, wellbeing, safety, and

5514
06:00:59.884 --> 06:01:03.424
connection, and of the devastating consequences

5515
06:01:03.564 --> 06:01:06.664
when systems that are actually in place to support

5516
06:01:06.674 --> 06:01:10.244
people fail the people that they're there to support.

5517
06:01:12.464 --> 06:01:16.214
When people lose access to stable housing, the impacts are felt across

5518
06:01:16.264 --> 06:01:20.144
every aspect of their lives, and that is why homelessness must

5519
06:01:20.184 --> 06:01:23.834
be addressed as a housing, health, and wellbeing issue, and

5520
06:01:23.864 --> 06:01:27.784
not as a public order issue. Those connections to

5521
06:01:27.804 --> 06:01:31.344
health, housing, and social services are vital

5522
06:01:31.384 --> 06:01:35.254
lifelines to get people like Caitlin the support that they

5523
06:01:35.284 --> 06:01:35.584
need.

5524
06:01:37.154 --> 06:01:40.384
This bill prioritizes enforcement over care,

5525
06:01:40.584 --> 06:01:44.024
displacement over housing, and punishment over prevention.

5526
06:01:44.864 --> 06:01:48.744
This is actually about people's lives, their dignity, their safety,

5527
06:01:49.054 --> 06:01:50.964
their health, and their right to belong.

5528
06:01:51.664 --> 06:01:55.654
It's about someone's daughter, someone's sister, auntie, mother, or

5529
06:01:55.684 --> 06:01:56.194
grandmother.

5530
06:01:57.604 --> 06:02:01.424
On these grounds, we respectfully ask the committee to reconsider

5531
06:02:01.483 --> 06:02:05.464
and withdraw this bill in its entirety, and instead, we urge the

5532
06:02:05.484 --> 06:02:09.414
government to focus on the long-term solutions that will end women's

5533
06:02:09.464 --> 06:02:10.204
homelessness.

5534
06:02:10.644 --> 06:02:14.584
Thank

5535
06:02:14.644 --> 06:02:16.184
you, Amanda and Victoria.

